   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*Pese a que* (despite the fact that) is another close relative of *aunque* and *a pesar de que*, and takes the subjunctive under the same rule -- ideal for a closing lesson that wants to honor a real achievement while immediately naming its real limits. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know *a pesar de* + noun or infinitive and *a pesar de que* + a full clause from B1 Unit 32. They admit a difficulty and go on. They are the right tool for the balance of industrialisation: real achievements, but also real limits."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Pese a que resultara imposible imaginar, en 1930, un continente capaz de fabricar acero y automóviles, esa transformación se había convertido en una realidad consolidada hacia los años sesenta.",
-          "english": "Despite it being impossible to imagine, in 1930, a continent capable of manufacturing steel and cars, that transformation had become a consolidated reality by the 1960s."
+          "spanish": "A pesar de estos logros, la región tenía problemas.",
+          "english": "Despite these achievements, the region had problems."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Pese a que este logro industrial resultara genuinamente impresionante, varios economistas señalaron problemas estructurales serios.",
-          "english": "Despite this industrial achievement being genuinely impressive, several economists pointed to serious structural problems."
+          "spanish": "A pesar de que el Estado ayudaba a la industria, las exportaciones seguían siendo materias primas.",
+          "english": "Although the state helped industry, exports were still mostly raw materials."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Pese a que la industrialización había transformado radicalmente ciudades como São Paulo, el desarrollo se concentró desproporcionadamente en unas pocas regiones.",
-          "english": "Despite industrialization having radically transformed cities like São Paulo, development was concentrated disproportionately in a few regions."
+          "spanish": "A pesar del crecimiento de las ciudades, la desigualdad entre regiones no desapareció.",
+          "english": "Despite the growth of the cities, the inequality between regions did not disappear."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Pese a que la industrialización latinoamericana representara un logro histórico genuino, las semillas de futuras dificultades ya estaban sembradas dentro de su propio éxito.",
-          "english": "Despite Latin American industrialization representing a genuine historical achievement, the seeds of future difficulties were already sown within its own success."
+          "spanish": "A pesar de ser pequeño, el mercado interno permitió crecer a muchas fábricas.",
+          "english": "Although it was small, the home market let many factories grow."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "*Pese a* (without que) works directly before a noun -- *pese a las dificultades* -- exactly like *a pesar de* and *debido a*; the que version always introduces a full clause with its own conjugated verb."
+      "content": "After *a pesar de* put a noun or an infinitive (*a pesar de los límites*, *a pesar de ser pequeño*). Before a full verb use *a pesar de que* (*a pesar de que ayudaba*). Remember *de* + *el* = *del*: *a pesar del crecimiento*."
