   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*Se suele* + infinitive (it's usually / it's typically) is the impersonal way to state a general pattern or convention without naming who holds it -- exactly the tool needed to summarize how scholars typically define and describe a contested term like populism. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "content": "You know impersonal *se* from B1 Unit 6: *se* + a third-person verb says what is said or done in general, without naming anyone (*Se habla español aquí*). You also know *soler* from B1 Unit 5. Together they give *se suele* + infinitive: \"it is usually …\". Historians use it to report how a disputed word is normally used, because populism has no single definition."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
       "items": [
